{
  "_doc": [
    "Regions to segment per statue for blender/paint_statues.py (prompts only; colours live in polychromy_palette.json).",
    "Each region: name (used for the colour lookup), kind (skin, hair, beard, garment, attribute, support, sandals, plinth),",
    "prompts (GroundingDINO phrases; masks of all prompts are pooled), views (body, head or both), threshold (detector score),",
    "rank: overrides the priority of the region's kind when masks overlap (order: beard 0, hair 1, sandals 2, skin 3, attribute 4, plinth 5, support 6, garment 7; e.g. 0.5 for a helmet over hair).",
    "zmin_face: lowest point of the region in face heights above the eye line (e.g. 0.55 keeps a helmet off the hair at the temples).",
    "zmin_rel / zmax_rel: height range of the region as a fraction of the statue height (defaults per kind: plinth <0.3, beard >0.5, sandals <0.2).",
    "vote (fraction of the views that see a vertex which must agree; default 0.35), max_mask_frac (largest mask, as a fraction of the silhouette; default per kind).",
    "A statue's list replaces 'default_regions' entirely unless it sets \"inherit\": true, in which case its regions are added",
    "to the defaults and regions with the same name override them. Keys not listed here use default_regions.",
    "Optional 'hints': list of {region, centre [x,y,z] in metres, radius} spheres that force a label (manual fixes).",
    "Optional 'beard': false removes the beard region; 'face': false skips eyes, brows and lips."
  ],
